{
  "$schema": "../../schema/markup.schema.json",
  "version": "0.1.0",
  "id": "page",
  "kind": "view",
  "summary": "A builder page. Its file also draws the document skeleton every view sits in, once.",
  "root": {
    "element": "html",
    "note": "The whole document: head, then body."
  },
  "elements": [
    {
      "role": "head",
      "element": "head",
      "note": "Only what the contract fixes; each platform writes the rest of head natively.",
      "children": [
        {
          "role": "scriptless",
          "element": "noscript",
          "optional": true,
          "when": "the site header is drawn",
          "children": [
            {
              "role": "scriptless-style",
              "element": "style",
              "text": ".salt-header{--salt-header-phone-menu:inline-flex;--salt-header-phone-burger:none;--salt-header-phone-wrap:wrap}"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "body",
      "element": "body",
      "children": [
        {
          "role": "skip-link",
          "element": "a",
          "classes": [
            "salt-skip-link"
          ],
          "attributes": {
            "href": "#main"
          },
          "text": "from:labels.skip"
        },
        {
          "role": "consent-banner",
          "element": "div",
          "classes": [
            "salt-consent-banner"
          ],
          "attributes": {
            "role": "region",
            "aria-label": "from:labels.region"
          },
          "optional": true,
          "when": "consent is pending and the site runs an integration that needs it",
          "children": [
            {
              "role": "consent-message",
              "element": "div",
              "classes": [
                "salt-consent-banner__message"
              ],
              "text": "from:message"
            },
            {
              "role": "consent-actions",
              "element": "div",
              "classes": [
                "salt-consent-banner__actions"
              ],
              "children": [
                {
                  "role": "consent-choice",
                  "component": "button",
                  "repeat": {
                    "from": "accept, reject, preferences",
                    "max": 3
                  }
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "consent-announce",
          "element": "p",
          "classes": [
            "salt-sr-only"
          ],
          "attributes": {
            "role": "status",
            "aria-live": "polite"
          },
          "optional": true,
          "when": "the consent banner is offered"
        },
        {
          "role": "header",
          "component": "site-header"
        },
        {
          "role": "main",
          "element": "main",
          "attributes": {
            "id": "main",
            "tabindex": "-1"
          },
          "children": [
            {
              "role": "fallback-heading",
              "component": "fallback-heading",
              "optional": true,
              "when": "no section claimed the h1"
            },
            {
              "role": "sections",
              "component": "section",
              "repeat": {
                "from": "page sections"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "footer",
          "component": "site-footer"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "headings": {
    "provides": "always",
    "role": "main",
    "level": "plan",
    "note": "The first heading-providing section claims the h1; otherwise fallback-heading draws it.",
    "rules": [
      "section#single-h1",
      "section#fallback-heading"
    ]
  },
  "script": {
    "kind": "none"
  },
  "uses": [
    "site-header",
    "site-footer",
    "fallback-heading",
    "section",
    "button"
  ],
  "ruleRefs": [
    "section#landmarks",
    "section#single-h1"
  ],
  "hooks": [
    {
      "class": "salt-skip-link",
      "role": "skip-link",
      "reason": "New: the skip link's class. The shared stylesheets owe the visually-hidden-until-focused rule."
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    {
      "topic": "ruling",
      "text": "The consent banner is drawn only when the site runs an integration that needs consent (SC-006). Salt for WordPress ports Salt for Next.js's banner, gate, preferences panel, categories and cookie format; a client that needs a certified consent tool (Google Ads personalisation in the UK and EEA) uses one as a Grain override."
    },
    {
      "topic": "ruling",
      "text": "The scriptless phone layout is the noscript style in head: with no script it keeps the header's menu and call to action on screen below the breakpoint, hides the burger nothing could open, and lets the row wrap, through the three custom properties chrome.css reads. It sits in head because a style element inside noscript is conforming only there; a no-js class removed by script was rejected because it needs a blocking script and leaves a phone whose script fails mid-page with no menu."
    }
  ],
  "platforms": {
    "nextjs": {
      "formerly": [
        {
          "role": "skip-link",
          "element": "a",
          "classes": [
            "skip-link"
          ],
          "note": "apps/example layout"
        },
        {
          "role": "main",
          "element": "main",
          "attributes": [
            "id=main",
            "tabindex=-1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "owes": [
        "Rename skip-link to salt-skip-link (and give it a rule in chrome.css).",
        "The header's noscript style in the document head, moved from inside the header."
      ]
    },
    "wordpress": {
      "formerly": [
        {
          "role": "skip-link",
          "element": "a",
          "classes": [
            "visually-hidden"
          ]
        },
        {
          "role": "main",
          "element": "main",
          "attributes": [
            "id=main"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "owes": [
        "salt-skip-link; tabindex -1 on main; the hidden h1 as fallback-heading; the consent banner, gate, preferences panel, categories and cookie format ported from Salt for Next.js, drawn only when an integration needs consent (SC-006).",
        "The header's noscript style in the document head (wp_head)."
      ]
    }
  }
}
